    "summary": "Qualified both-family production routes, complete source and test scope equivalence, independent-session cancellation, native/progress write isolation, context/history tampering, source capacity, migration/runtime write windows and cleanup crash recovery. Corrected design publication-only recovery after worker reclamation and fresh daemon startup: reuse permanent owned head proof while retaining original baseline and feedback, never dispatching a reviewer. Round 1's only rejected assertion is corrected: a controlled real Claude-stream tool-start event must durably advance BOTH runtime sequence and lastMeaningfulActivityAt for code and design while checkpoint bytes, inode and mtime remain identical and leases remain unchanged. The corrected crash/native fixture and publication decision-validation regression passed locally; production implementation is unchanged since 19502a779. Round 2's remaining gap is covered by eight passing production migration/crash cases: each family and historical v1/v2, killed before upgrade or after canonical upgrade before bind/activation. Actual production ReviewWorkerPreparation.open performs migration; only the test worker is terminated at the boundary. Cases verify original source digest, unchanged previous records and closed guard audit, exact sequence-zero runtime retention with no new admission, read-only observation, then explicit resubmission preserving runtime identity to successful publication. No production implementation changed for these qualification corrections. The latest remaining t7/t8 gap is now repeated through unmodified production defaults in review-production-route-invariants.test.ts: missing BUILD before admission; all mismatched role sets and foreign workflow/epic/issue/story documents; pinned packet immutability and publication after mutable route removal; broken Epic/missing seed/orphan bugfix ancestry; invalid identity, author, containment, kind and oversized document rejection; actual successful plan phase after unrelated edit followed by required-HLD mutation invalidation; and completed first/correction impact attempts across Epic, standalone, issue correction-link and seeded workflows preserving prior feedback and required reference roles. All six added cases passed locally in focused batches; implementation remains unchanged since 19502a779.",
